      "raw_text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 4 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Shear Line\nIssued at: 2:00 AM, 25 November 2025(Tuesday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Quezon, Laguna, Rizal, Metro Manila, Cavite, Batangas, Bulacan and Nueva Ecija(General Tinio, Bongabon, Palayan, Gabaldon, Laur, Gapan, Penaranda).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: Possible FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate with occasional heavy rains over Zambales and Bataan within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Tarlac, Pampanga and Nueva Ecija(Cabiao, San Antonio, San Isidro, Aliaga, Cabanatuan, Carranglan, Cuyapo, General Mamerto Natividad, Guimba, Jaen, Licab, Llanera, Lupao, Nampicuan, Pantabangan, Quezon, Rizal, San Jose, San Leonardo, Santa Rosa, Santo Domingo, Munoz, Talavera, Talugtug, Zaragoza) which may persist within 3 hours.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 5:00 AM today.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
      "cleaned_text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 4 #NCR_PRSD Weather System: Shear Line Issued at: 2:00 AM, 25 November 2025(Tuesday) YELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Quezon, Laguna, Rizal, Metro Manila, Cavite, Batangas, Bulacan and Nueva Ecija(General Tinio, Bongabon, Palayan, Gabaldon, Laur, Gapan, Penaranda). ASSOCIATED HAZARD: Possible FLOODING in flood-prone areas. Meanwhile, expect light to moderate with occasional heavy rains over Zambales and Bataan within the next 3 hours. Light to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Tarlac, Pampanga and Nueva Ecija(Cabiao, San Antonio, San Isidro, Aliaga, Cabanatuan, Carranglan, Cuyapo, General Mamerto Natividad, Guimba, Jaen, Licab, Llanera, Lupao, Nampicuan, Pantabangan, Quezon, Rizal, San Jose, San Leonardo, Santa Rosa, Santo Domingo, Munoz, Talavera, Talugtug, Zaragoza) which may persist within 3 hours. The public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 5:00 AM today. For more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to",
      "english_translation": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 4 #CR_PD Weather System: Shear Line Issued and: 2:00 AM, 25 November25(uesday) YEWING LEVEn: Quegon, Rizzal, Manila, Baby, Bulkace and Nucinetaéste, Palagbongo, Lezalon, Zacanda, Apanda, Childas, Busket.",
